From: Florent Revest <revestflo@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wlan: mgmt_txrx: don't hold a system wakelock for pending mgmt
 tx (let S2R arm WoW)

On aurora (Pixel Watch 2, Halium-13 + lipstick compositor + autosleep) the
watch relies on system suspend (S2R) to save power off-charger. The qcacld
mgmt_txrx layer takes a system (S2R-blocking) wakelock "mgmt_txrx tx_cmp"
whenever a management frame TX is pending completion (up to 300ms).

The WLAN wiphy .suspend callback (hdd_suspend_wlan) itself transmits a few
802.11 power-save / WoW-transition management frames as part of arming suspend.
The tx_cmp system wakelock those frames raise then trips pm_wakeup_pending() on
the very next device in the dpm_suspend order (kgsl-smmu) and aborts the
suspend BEFORE it reaches WMI_WOW_ENABLE. WoW never arms, the rollback-resume
re-sends the transition frames, and the next attempt aborts the same way -- a
self-perpetuating storm (~100mA, watch never sleeps). Confirmed on HW: when a
suspend occasionally wins the race and arms WoW, mgmt tx stops and the watch
deep-sleeps cleanly and permanently.

Drop only the SYSTEM wakelock for pending mgmt tx; keep the runtime-PM lock
(wakelock_tx_runtime_cmp) so WLAN runtime-PM is unaffected. Firmware buffers
mgmt tx-completion across S2R and delivers it on resume, so nothing is lost.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [aurora-specific; upstream would gate this behind
a config option -- the system wakelock is intentional for non-autosleep hosts]
Signed-off-by: Florent Revest <revestflo@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/private/msm-google-modules/wlan/qca-wifi-host-cmn/umac/cmn_services/mgmt_txrx/core/src/wlan_mgmt_txrx_main.c b/private/msm-google-modules/wlan/qca-wifi-host-cmn/umac/cmn_services/mgmt_txrx/core/src/wlan_mgmt_txrx_main.c
--- a/private/msm-google-modules/wlan/qca-wifi-host-cmn/umac/cmn_services/mgmt_txrx/core/src/wlan_mgmt_txrx_main.c
+++ b/private/msm-google-modules/wlan/qca-wifi-host-cmn/umac/cmn_services/mgmt_txrx/core/src/wlan_mgmt_txrx_main.c
@@ -126,9 +126,19 @@ struct mgmt_txrx_desc_elem_t *wlan_mgmt_txrx_desc_get(
 
 	qdf_spin_unlock_bh(&mgmt_txrx_pdev_ctx->mgmt_desc_pool.desc_pool_lock);
 
-	/* acquire the wakelock when there are pending mgmt tx frames */
-	qdf_wake_lock_timeout_acquire(&mgmt_txrx_pdev_ctx->wakelock_tx_cmp,
-				      MGMT_TXRX_WAKELOCK_TIMEOUT_TX_CMP);
+	/*
+	 * aurora: do NOT take the system (S2R) wakelock for a pending mgmt tx.
+	 * On this autosleep/Halium watch the lipstick compositor keeps the GPU
+	 * fd open, so the SoC relies on system suspend (S2R) to save power. The
+	 * WLAN wiphy .suspend callback (hdd_suspend_wlan) itself transmits a few
+	 * 802.11 power-save/WoW-transition mgmt frames; the tx_cmp system wakelock
+	 * those raise then trips pm_wakeup_pending() on the very next device in
+	 * the dpm_suspend order and aborts the suspend BEFORE it can send
+	 * WMI_WOW_ENABLE. WoW never arms, the rollback-resume re-sends the frames,
+	 * and the suspend attempt self-perpetuates (~100mA, never sleeps). Keeping
+	 * only the runtime-PM lock lets the first S2R complete and arm WoW;
+	 * firmware buffers mgmt tx-completion across S2R and delivers it on resume.
+	 */
 	qdf_runtime_pm_prevent_suspend(
 		&mgmt_txrx_pdev_ctx->wakelock_tx_runtime_cmp);
 
@@ -170,10 +180,11 @@ void wlan_mgmt_txrx_desc_put(
 	qdf_spin_unlock_bh(&mgmt_txrx_pdev_ctx->mgmt_desc_pool.desc_pool_lock);
 
 	if (release_wakelock) {
+		/* aurora: system tx_cmp wakelock is no longer taken (see
+		 * wlan_mgmt_txrx_desc_get); only drop the runtime-PM lock here.
+		 */
 		qdf_runtime_pm_allow_suspend(
 			&mgmt_txrx_pdev_ctx->wakelock_tx_runtime_cmp);
-		qdf_wake_lock_release(&mgmt_txrx_pdev_ctx->wakelock_tx_cmp,
-				      MGMT_TXRX_WAKELOCK_REASON_TX_CMP);
 	}
 }
 
